            "peakPromptTokens": 2767,
            "latencyMs": 59953,
            "replyText": "Stopping a container in YCP (or Docker) **does not delete its data**. The container's filesystem remains intact, but it transitions to a stopped state. Data persists unless explicitly removed via:\n- Deleting the container (which removes all associated data)\n- Removing volumes (if the container uses persistent storage like named volumes or host directories)\n\nThis behavior aligns with standard Docker practices. For example, if you stop a container named `my-app`, its data stays until you manually delete it or its volumes.",
            "recordedAt": "2026-09-28T21:46:41.417Z",
